  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Morning Sky",
    "overview": "The day is a sky. A gradient band across the top of every screen follows the real hour, the sun crosses a dashed arc from 5 AM to midnight, and each of today's doses sits on that arc at its own time. Everything below the sky is cloud-white panels on a pale sky ground, set in one navy ink. The world is calm, kind and plain: one obvious action per screen, large type, generous space, and nothing that needs decoding.\n\nState is never carried by colour alone. Every dose state has a form as well as words: a solid mark is done, a dashed mark is waiting, a ring means act now, a strike means skipped. The only warm colour is the sun, and it means \"now\". Red is kept back for the STOP button and for real alerts, so that when it appears it is believed.\n\nThe world replaces the retired pharmacy-label look (labels, stickers, identical white pill-app cards). It is rendered with soft neutral elevation, rounded cloud panels and a single typeface, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, self-hosted.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A sky band keyed to the real hour (dawn, day, dusk, night) holds the top bar, the sun's arc and the greeting.",
      "Cloud-white panels (24px corners; the due dose 28px) on a pale sky ground, with soft navy-tinted shadows.",
      "One ink navy for type and primary actions; the warm sun only for \"now\"; red only for STOP and real alerts.",
      "State in form plus words: solid done, dashed waiting, ringed act now, struck skipped.",
      "One typeface on a four-step scale that grows with the user's Display text size.",
      "A plain black-on-white high-contrast mode with no sky."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Sun Means Now Rule",
        "body": "The warm sun palette appears only on the sun itself and on whatever is happening now. A thing that is not current never turns warm.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Believed Rule",
        "body": "Red is STOP and real alerts, nothing else. A destructive but ordinary action (the danger button) is drawn in ink, not red; the build recoloured it for exactly this reason.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pills Are Data Rule",
        "body": "A medicine's colour swatch shows the real pill's colour from its label. It is data, not palette, and is exempt from the colour jobs above.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Steps Rule",
        "body": "There are four type steps (small, body, lead, title), all in rem. The user's Display text size scales the root (112.5%, 125%, 143.75%), so every step and icon grows with it. Do not add steps or set type in px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Cloud Rule",
        "body": "Elevation is soft and blurred, tinted with the ink navy. No hard offset shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Ring Rule",
        "body": "One ringed action per screen, and it is the primary action. If a screen has two ringed things, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** key the sky band to the real hour through `html[data-sky]` (dawn, day, dusk, night) and keep type on the band in the sky ink pair.",
      "**Do** give every state a form and words: solid done, dashed waiting, ringed act now, struck skipped, alert colour for missed or uncertain.",
      "**Do** ring exactly one action per screen, the primary one.",
      "**Do** keep the corner ladder: panels 24px (due panel 28px), insets 18px, controls 14px, chips and STOP full pill.",
      "**Do** set all type in the four rem steps (small .875rem, body 1rem, lead 1.3rem, title 2.25rem) and icons at 1.3rem or 1.7rem, so the Display text sizes scale everything.",
      "**Do** keep targets at 48px or more and STOP always visible and isolated.",
      "**Do** let the sun stand for a dose due at the sun, and move any other dose clear of it along the arc rather than overlapping.",
      "**Do** keep high contrast plain: black on white, no sky, 2px borders, underlined quiet actions."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use red for anything but STOP and real alerts; draw ordinary destructive actions in ink.",
      "**Don't** use the warm sun colours for anything that is not the sun or happening now.",
      "**Don't** carry state by colour alone.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface, a fifth type step, or px font sizes.",
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows; elevation is soft and navy-tinted.",
      "**Don't** return to label-and-sticker chrome or a list of identical white pill cards."
    ]
  }
}